# What each profile of TestGenerated of the driver check must reach: see stmttest.Reached.
# A kind on a line. A kind that no run reaches three times fails the test. The texts that the
# test excuses from the comparison, the kinds that begin with "excused: ", are pinned exactly
# and are not listed here.

# Each kind of statement by its outcome, and each call, with arguments and without.
createtable ok
createtable already exists
createtable no rows
createtable wrong number of arguments
insert ok
insert UNIQUE constraint failed
insert has no column named
insert no such table
insert no rows
insert wrong number of arguments
insert with a parameter ok
insert with a parameter UNIQUE constraint failed
insert with a parameter no such table
insert with a parameter wrong number of arguments
insert with a parameter argument of a type not supported
insert with a parameter named argument
select ok
select ok with rows
select no such table
select no rows
select wrong number of arguments
droptable ok
droptable no such table
other not supported
other syntax error
other incomplete input
begin ok
call exec
call query
call prepare, exec
call prepare, query
call query row
call begin
call prepare, exec several times
call exec with arguments
call query with arguments
call prepare, exec with arguments
call prepare, query with arguments
call query row with arguments
call prepare, exec several times with arguments

# Write transactions that commit and that roll back, on a pinned connection and through the
# pool, after a failed call, an insert, a create table, and a drop table, and while rows of
# theirs are open.
write transaction begin ok
call begin in a transaction
write transaction commit ok on a pinned connection
write transaction commit ok through the pool
write transaction rollback ok on a pinned connection
write transaction rollback ok through the pool
write transaction commit ok after a failed call
write transaction rollback ok after a failed call
write transaction commit ok after an insert
write transaction rollback ok after an insert
write transaction commit ok after a create table
write transaction rollback ok after a create table
write transaction commit ok after a drop table
write transaction rollback ok after a drop table
write transaction commit ok while rows are open
write transaction rollback ok while rows are open

# Each call in a write transaction, with arguments, and what it gives.
write transaction: call exec with arguments
write transaction: call query with arguments
write transaction: call query row with arguments
write transaction: call prepare, exec with arguments
write transaction: call prepare, query with arguments
write transaction: call prepare, exec several times with arguments
write transaction: call prepare outside, exec in the transaction with arguments
write transaction: call prepare outside, query in the transaction with arguments
write transaction: call query, rows left open
write transaction: call query beside the transaction
write transaction: insert ok
write transaction: insert with a parameter ok
write transaction: insert UNIQUE constraint failed
write transaction: insert no such table
write transaction: createtable ok
write transaction: createtable already exists
write transaction: droptable ok
write transaction: droptable no such table
write transaction: other syntax error
write transaction: insert with a parameter wrong number of arguments
write transaction: insert with a parameter argument of a type not supported
write transaction: select ok with rows after a write of the transaction
write transaction: rows left open
write transaction: insert while rows are open
write transaction: select while rows are open

# Through the pool, a query outside a write transaction, which must not see its changes.
beside a write transaction: select ok with rows

# Read-only transactions: their queries, and their writes, which are refused, also an insert
# with a parameter and without one while rows of the transaction are open.
read-only transaction begin ok
read-only transaction commit ok on a pinned connection
read-only transaction commit ok through the pool
read-only transaction rollback ok on a pinned connection
read-only transaction rollback ok through the pool
read-only transaction: select ok with rows
read-only transaction: rows left open
read-only transaction: insert attempt to write a readonly database
read-only transaction: insert with a parameter attempt to write a readonly database
read-only transaction: createtable attempt to write a readonly database
read-only transaction: droptable attempt to write a readonly database
read-only transaction: insert no such table
read-only transaction: createtable already exists
read-only transaction: call prepare outside, exec in the transaction
read-only transaction: call prepare outside, query in the transaction
read-only transaction: call prepare, exec several times with arguments
call begin read-only in a transaction
read-only transaction: insert while rows are open
read-only transaction: insert with a parameter while rows are open

# Each type as a key, with an insert that succeeds, meets a key that exists, has a value of
# another type, and is refused in a read-only transaction; each kind of literal and of
# argument, also those that no column holds.
reached: insert into INT ok
reached: insert into INTEGER ok
reached: insert into REAL ok
reached: insert into TEXT ok
reached: insert into BLOB ok
reached: insert into INT UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: insert into INTEGER UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: insert into REAL UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: insert into TEXT UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: insert into BLOB UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: insert into INT a value of another type
reached: insert into INTEGER a value of another type
reached: insert into REAL a value of another type
reached: insert into TEXT a value of another type
reached: insert into BLOB a value of another type
reached: insert into INT attempt to write a readonly database
reached: insert into INTEGER attempt to write a readonly database
reached: insert into REAL attempt to write a readonly database
reached: insert into TEXT attempt to write a readonly database
reached: insert into BLOB attempt to write a readonly database
reached: literal integer
reached: literal real
reached: literal real -0.0
reached: literal text
reached: literal empty text
reached: literal blob
reached: literal empty blob
reached: argument int64
reached: argument int
reached: argument int32
reached: argument uint64
reached: argument float64
reached: argument float64 -0.0
reached: argument float32
reached: argument string
reached: argument empty string
reached: argument []uint8
reached: argument empty []byte
reached: argument NaN
reached: argument infinite float64
reached: argument float32 that is not finite
reached: argument string that is not valid UTF-8
reached: argument string with NUL
reached: argument nil
reached: argument nil []byte
reached: argument bool
reached: argument time.Time
reached: argument uint64 above int64
reached: argument named

# Slice 5: inserts into tables of several columns, without a list and with one, with each
# fault and with two, also in a read-only transaction, and selects of * of each number of
# columns, of names, and of a name that the table does not have.
reached: insert without a list ok
reached: insert with a list ok
reached: insert without a list UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: insert with a list UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: insert with a list attempt to write a readonly database
reached: insert without a list attempt to write a readonly database
reached: insert with a column that the table does not have: has no column named
reached: insert with a column without a value: NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: insert with the wrong number of values: values were supplied
reached: insert with the wrong number of values:  values for 
reached: insert with a value of another type in the key: a value of another type
reached: insert with a value of another type in another column: a value of another type
reached: insert with two faults: NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: insert with two faults: a value of another type
reached: insert with two faults: has no column named
reached: insert with a column without a value: attempt to write a readonly database
reached: select * of 1 columns ok
reached: select * of 2 columns ok
reached: select * of 3 columns ok
reached: select of names ok
reached: select of a name that the table does not have no such column

# Slice 6: NULL as a literal and as each kind of nil that database/sql hands the driver as nil,
# in a column that takes it, also beside a key that exists and in a read-only transaction, and
# in the key and in a column that does not take it; each kind of a nil []byte, which s4ql
# refuses; a column that takes NULL left out of a list; NULL beside a value of another type in
# another column; and a select of * and of names with NULL among its values.
reached: literal null
reached: argument NULL as *int64
reached: argument NULL as *float64
reached: argument NULL as *string
reached: argument NULL as *[]uint8
reached: argument NULL as *sql.NullString
reached: argument NULL as sql.NullInt64
reached: argument NULL as sql.NullFloat64
reached: argument NULL as sql.NullString
reached: argument NULL as sql.Null[[]uint8]
reached: argument nil []byte as *[]uint8
reached: argument nil []byte as sql.Null[[]uint8]
reached: NULL literal into a column that takes NULL ok
reached: NULL argument into a column that takes NULL ok
reached: NULL literal into a column that takes NULL UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: NULL argument into a column that takes NULL UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: NULL literal into a column that takes NULL a value of another type
reached: NULL literal into the key NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: NULL argument into the key NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: NULL literal into a column that does not take NULL NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: NULL argument into a column that does not take NULL NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: insert that leaves out a column that takes NULL ok
reached: insert that leaves out a column that takes NULL UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: insert that leaves out a column that takes NULL a value of another type
reached: insert that leaves out a column that takes NULL NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: insert with NULL in the key: NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: insert with NULL in a column that does not take it: NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: insert of NULL beside a value of another type NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: insert of NULL beside a value of another type a value of another type
reached: select * with NULL ok
reached: select of names with NULL ok
reached: NULL literal into a column that takes NULL attempt to write a readonly database

# Slice 7: each operator on the key and on another column; each way that the plan reads rows;
# a select that gives no row, some rows, and every row of a table with rows; each kind of
# value, by literal and by argument, NULL by both; and the faults: a column that the table
# does not have, in a comparison and under IS NULL or IS NOT NULL, alone, before, and after
# other conditions, and in double quotes; a value of another type; arguments that s4ql
# refuses; a column tested twice; and contradicting conditions.
reached: = on the key ok
reached: != on the key ok
reached: < on the key ok
reached: <= on the key ok
reached: > on the key ok
reached: >= on the key ok
reached: IS NULL on the key ok
reached: IS NOT NULL on the key ok
reached: = on another column ok
reached: != on another column ok
reached: < on another column ok
reached: <= on another column ok
reached: > on another column ok
reached: >= on another column ok
reached: IS NULL on another column ok
reached: IS NOT NULL on another column ok
reached: WHERE that reads no row ok
reached: WHERE that reads a get of one key ok
reached: WHERE that reads a scan from a lower bound ok
reached: WHERE that reads a scan to an upper bound ok
reached: WHERE that reads a scan between two bounds ok
reached: WHERE that reads a scan between two bounds that hold no key ok
reached: WHERE that reads a scan of every row ok
reached: WHERE that gives no row of a table with rows
reached: WHERE that gives some rows of a table
reached: WHERE that gives every row of a table with rows
reached: comparison with literal integer ok
reached: comparison with literal real ok
reached: comparison with literal real -0.0 ok
reached: comparison with literal text ok
reached: comparison with literal empty text ok
reached: comparison with literal blob ok
reached: comparison with literal empty blob ok
reached: comparison with literal null ok
reached: comparison with argument int64 ok
reached: comparison with argument float64 ok
reached: comparison with argument float64 -0.0 ok
reached: comparison with argument string ok
reached: comparison with argument empty string ok
reached: comparison with argument []uint8 ok
reached: comparison with argument empty []byte ok
reached: comparison with argument nil ok
reached: WHERE with a column that the table does not have in a comparison, alone no such column
reached: WHERE with a column that the table does not have in a comparison, before other conditions no such column
reached: WHERE with a column that the table does not have in a comparison, after other conditions no such column
reached: WHERE with a column that the table does not have under IS NULL or IS NOT NULL, before other conditions no such column
reached: WHERE with a column that the table does not have under IS NULL or IS NOT NULL, after other conditions no such column
reached: WHERE with a column in double quotes that the table does not have no such column
reached: WHERE with a value of another type a value of another type
reached: WHERE with arguments that s4ql refuses not supported
reached: WHERE with arguments that s4ql refuses wrong number of arguments
reached: WHERE that tests a column more than once ok
reached: WHERE with contradicting conditions ok

# Slice 8: updates and deletes, each with and without WHERE, that change rows and that find
# none; refused in a read-only transaction; a change of the key that succeeds, meets a key
# that exists, and gets NULL; NULL for a column that does not take it; a column of SET or of
# WHERE that the table does not have, also in double quotes, which mattn's SQLite reads as a
# string; a value of another type in SET and in WHERE; arguments that s4ql refuses; ways that
# the scan reads the rows; and each table that an update or a delete changed, read back on
# both sides.
reached: update with WHERE ok, rows changed
reached: update with WHERE ok, no row found
reached: update without WHERE ok, rows changed
reached: update without WHERE ok, no row found
reached: delete with WHERE ok, rows changed
reached: delete with WHERE ok, no row found
reached: delete without WHERE ok, rows changed
reached: delete without WHERE ok, no row found
reached: update with WHERE attempt to write a readonly database
reached: delete with WHERE attempt to write a readonly database
reached: SET of the key ok, rows changed
reached: SET of the key UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: SET of the key NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: SET of NULL for a column that does not take it NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: SET of NULL for a column that does not take it ok, no row found
reached: SET of a column that the table does not have no such column
reached: SET of a column in double quotes that the table does not have no such column
reached: SET with a value of another type a value of another type
reached: SET with argument nil ok, no row found
reached: update WHERE with a column in double quotes that the table does not have no such column
reached: delete WHERE with a column in double quotes that the table does not have no such column
reached: update WHERE with a value of another type a value of another type
reached: delete WHERE with a value of another type a value of another type
reached: update with arguments that s4ql refuses not supported
reached: update with arguments that s4ql refuses wrong number of arguments
reached: delete with arguments that s4ql refuses not supported
reached: delete with arguments that s4ql refuses wrong number of arguments
reached: update WHERE that reads a get of one key ok, rows changed
reached: delete WHERE that reads a get of one key ok, rows changed
reached: delete WHERE that reads a scan from a lower bound ok, rows changed
reached: delete WHERE that reads a scan to an upper bound ok, rows changed
reached: update WHERE that reads a scan of every row ok, rows changed
reached: update WHERE that reads no row ok, no row found
reached: table read back after an update or a delete
reached: SET with literal null ok, rows changed

# Slice 9: each outcome of a create index, of a drop index, and of a create table that meets
# an index, by the kind of the statement and of the error, also in a read-only transaction,
# which refuses both.
createindex ok
createindex no such table
createindex already exists
createindex there is already a table named
createindex no such column
createindex attempt to write a readonly database
dropindex ok
dropindex no such index
dropindex attempt to write a readonly database
createtable there is already an index named

# Slice 10: each of the four statements with IF NOT EXISTS or IF EXISTS that did its work,
# that did nothing for each reason of stmttest.ExistsRule, and that gave each error, as
# pair.reachExists counts them, also in a read-only transaction, which refuses one that
# would write.
reached: create table if not exists did its work
reached: create table if not exists did nothing: a table of the name exists
reached: create table if not exists duplicate column name
reached: create table if not exists there is already an index named
reached: create table if not exists attempt to write a readonly database
reached: drop table if exists did its work
reached: drop table if exists did nothing: no table of the name exists
reached: drop table if exists did nothing: no table of the name exists, and an index has it
reached: drop table if exists attempt to write a readonly database
reached: create index if not exists did its work
reached: create index if not exists did nothing: an index of the name exists
reached: create index if not exists no such table
reached: create index if not exists there is already a table named
reached: create index if not exists no such column
reached: create index if not exists attempt to write a readonly database
reached: drop index if exists did its work
reached: drop index if exists did nothing: no index of the name exists
reached: drop index if exists did nothing: no index of the name exists, and a table has it

# Slice 11: inserts that leave out a column and store its default of each type, also of the
# key, and DEFAULT NULL in a column that takes NULL; NOT NULL from a DEFAULT NULL in a column
# that does not take NULL and in the key; UNIQUE from a default of the key; the refusal of a
# read-only transaction before the default; and an explicit NULL for a column with a default.
# The driver check runs under SQLite's default length limit, so a record that a long default
# makes too long is required of TestDifferential of the engine only.
reached: insert that leaves out a column with a default of integer ok
reached: insert that leaves out a column with a default of real ok
reached: insert that leaves out a column with a default of text ok
reached: insert that leaves out a column with a default of blob ok
reached: insert that leaves out the key with a default ok
reached: insert that leaves out the key with a default UNIQUE constraint failed
reached: insert that leaves out a column that takes NULL with DEFAULT NULL ok
reached: insert that leaves out a column that does not take NULL with DEFAULT NULL NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: insert that leaves out the key with DEFAULT NULL NOT NULL constraint failed
reached: insert that leaves out a column with a default of integer attempt to write a readonly database
reached: NULL given for a column with a default, which takes NULL ok
reached: NULL given for a column with a default, which does not take NULL NOT NULL constraint failed

